      "message": "I think this is good, but it could actually trigger a behavior change, because the old versions were using the `f` suffixed functions (eg, implicitly cast double-to-float ... stupid macros). Now we might end up calling the double or int version of some of these? Two ideas:\n\n1) Can we just remove these entirely (eg, replace them at the call-site with the std:: calls). That\u0027s probably time-consuming, though, and then we have to be sure at each call-site that we\u0027re really passing a float.\n2) Change these to be inline wrapper functions, so we at least get the argument coercion to float.",
